@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@
+# Native Scarlet AOT bringup
+
+The in-tree backend uses Cranelift 0.127.0 and keeps its normal Rust `dylib`
+entry point, `__rustc_codegen_backend`. Build it with the same compiler source
+and sysroot as the native Scarlet rustc driver: the Rust ABI is not stable across
+compiler versions. This is an AOT path; JIT and its libc/memory-mapping dependencies
+are not needed. Do not enable `jit` or `unstable-features` for the native build.
+
+The patched target-lexicon 0.13.3 package in
+`native-host-deps/target-lexicon-0.13.3` recognizes Scarlet explicitly. Both its
+build script and the backend's target parsing preserve the real Scarlet triple,
+ELF format, System V calling convention and LP64 data model. Its manifest patch
+is local to this backend workspace so Cargo vendoring can preserve that source.
+
+`cranelift-native` is excluded when the backend itself runs on Scarlet. It pulls
+in libc on RISC-V hosts for CPU discovery, which Scarlet does not use. Leave
+`-Ctarget-cpu=native` unset; requesting it produces an explicit unsupported
+message. AOT ISA selection still uses the requested Scarlet target architecture.
+
+Full compiler/backend builds belong in the Scarlet Rust Nix GitHub Actions job.
+Once that job prepares a matching build-host compiler and Scarlet rustc private
+libraries, the bootstrap backend step is:
+
+```sh
+python3 x.py build --stage 1 --host aarch64-unknown-scarlet \
+  --target aarch64-unknown-scarlet compiler/rustc_codegen_cranelift
+```
+
+The cross-host bootstrap configuration and linker must already be present. For
+RV64 use `riscv64gc-unknown-scarlet`. No local full compiler build is required for
+the source patch checks.
+
+For the first guest code generation proof, compile an asm-free function using
+an existing matching Scarlet `core` sysroot:
+
+```rust
+#![no_std]
+#[unsafe(no_mangle)]
+pub extern "C" fn answer() -> i32 { 42 }
+```
+
+```sh
+rustc answer.rs --crate-type lib --emit=obj -Cpanic=abort \
+  -Ccodegen-units=1 -Cdebuginfo=0 --target aarch64-unknown-scarlet \
+  --sysroot /system/rust -Zcodegen-backend=cranelift -o answer.o
+```
+
+This emits a real ELF object without calling an assembler or linker. Linking and
+running that object inside Scarlet is a separate required validation step.
+
+Nonempty inline/global assembly needs an external native GNU-compatible
+assembler. On Scarlet the backend runs `as`, or the path selected by `CG_CLIF_AS`.
+It never recursively selects an unavailable LLVM backend. A missing assembler
+produces an actionable code-generation error. Other hosts retain the existing
+LLVM-assisted assembly path unless `CG_CLIF_AS` or the build-time
+`CG_CLIF_FORCE_GNU_AS` option explicitly selects external assembly. A native
+assembler is not provided by this patch; Scarlet's current source tree does not
+contain one.
